            <ArticleTitle>Fasting may not be required before percutaneous coronary intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/eb-2014-101904</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Implications for practice and research: The results of this study suggest that percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) can be safely conducted without preprocedural fasting. Revision is needed of current fasting protocols. The findings of Hamid and colleagues must be confirmed by further randomised trials.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
